From: grimtickle-overlay <overlay@grimtickle.local>
Date: Wed, 02 Jul 2026 23:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Gentoo: remove proxmox-apt "cache" feature — no libapt-pkg on Gentoo

The "cache" feature of the proxmox-apt crate enables FFI bindings against
Debian's libapt-pkg C library (via the apt-pkg crate). libapt-pkg does not
exist in the Gentoo portage tree and is Debian/Ubuntu-only.

Remove the "cache" feature from pve-rs's Cargo.toml dependency entry.
Without it, the APT repository list/add/change functions still compile
(they manipulate .sources.list files in pure Rust), but the cache-dependent
functions (list_available_apt_update, update_database) are not built.

The companion patch stubs those functions at the Rust export level so that
perlmod-generated XS bindings still compile and return a clear error when
called from Perl (which they are not, since PVE::API2::APT is also stubbed).

---
 pve-rs/Cargo.toml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pve-rs/Cargo.toml b/pve-rs/Cargo.toml
--- a/pve-rs/Cargo.toml
+++ b/pve-rs/Cargo.toml
@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@ crate-type = ["cdylib"]
 perlmod = { version = "0.13.5", features = ["exporter"] }
 
-proxmox-apt = { version = "0.11.5", features = ["cache"] }
+proxmox-apt = { version = "0.11.5" }
 proxmox-apt-api-types = "1.0"
 proxmox-config-digest = "0.1"
